  "title": "Operational K9 Equipment Reference",
  "markdown": "# Operational K9 Equipment Reference\n\n![Visual reference from Operational K9 Equipment Reference](../../assets/figures/page-0222-visual.webp)\n\n| Vascular Access | Size | Length |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| IM | 20 g | 1 inch |\n| SC | 18 - 20 g | 1.5 inch |\n| IV | 18 g | 30 -32 mm |\n| IO | 15 g | 15 - 25 mm |\n\n> For GDV/Bloat - Must use forelimb for IV/IO access\n\n| Airway | Size |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| ETT | 10.0 - 12.0 mm |\n| Miller | 4 - 5 |\n| Cric | 8.0 mm |\n\n> **K9 ECG**\n>\n> May attach to:\n> a. Large Paw Pads\n> b. Axillary and inguinal\n> c. Distal limbs\n>\n> **KEY**: Electrodes must be in direct contact with skin:\n> CLIP HAIR\n\n| Needle Decompression (Chest or GDV) | |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 14 g | 3.25 inch |\n\nSubcutaneous Fluids\n\nEpaxials\n\nPelvis\n\nTriceps\n\nQuads\n\nRibs\n\nEpaxial Muscles\n\nPelvis\n\nIV Access (Front Leg)\n\nIV Access (Back Leg)\n\nDefib Pads (R / L)\n\nIntraosseous (EZ IO) Sites\n\nProximal Humerus\n\nMedial Tibia\n",
  "plain_text": "Operational K9 Equipment Reference Vascular Access Size Length IM 20 g 1 inch SC 18 - 20 g 1.5 inch IV 18 g 30 -32 mm IO 15 g 15 - 25 mm For GDV/Bloat - Must use forelimb for IV/IO access Airway Size ETT 10.0 - 12.0 mm Miller 4 - 5 Cric 8.0 mm K9 ECG May attach to: Large Paw Pads Axillary and inguinal Distal limbs KEY: Electrodes must be in direct contact with skin: CLIP HAIR Needle Decompression (Chest or GDV) 14 g 3.25 inch Subcutaneous Fluids Epaxials Pelvis Triceps Quads Ribs Epaxial Muscles Pelvis IV Access (Front Leg) IV Access (Back Leg) Defib Pads (R / L) Intraosseous (EZ IO) Sites Proximal Humerus Medial Tibia",
